  "scope": "Exact unchanged pinned Debian Firefox ESR ARM64, software/headless Wayland at 100 percent scale; ordinary wrapped native textareas. Unsupported-zoom fallback/restoration is a boundary check, not native scaled support.",
  "implementation": {
    "provider": "Existing ordinary NSTextView/NSScrollView and shared NativeUI geometry/scroll API; no new control, provider, loader, transport or UI algorithm.",
    "geometry": "Real Gecko ScrollContainerFrame scroll port, computed document rectangle and layout-range boundaries consume native clip/document/bounds. DOM getters retain their existing engine rounding/zoom path.",
    "scroll": "Native offsets use original ScrollToCSSPixels/ScrollToImpl bookkeeping and trusted event lifecycle. The existing setter receives an exact acceptable native point after native rounding, avoiding a second fractional alignment phase.",
    "paint": "Existing complete native border-box snapshot. Offset transfer occurs during reflow/input, not painting. Engine child text/scrollers/resizer remain outside the owned native snapshot.",
    "selection": "Match the actual Selection through the live TextControlState selection controller; suppress only its competing hidden-editor caret scroll. Original queued event lifetime/cleanup remains. No copied caret geometry.",
    "lifetime": "Retain semantic nodes and revalidate native widget/frame identity after engine scrolling; reuse frame destruction/freezing/inactive cleanup. Reset inherited widget state in child processes.",
    "recovery": "Restore retained engine offset to recreated native object once per authenticated host generation after text synchronization; no input action replay.",
    "feature": "NEXTSPACE_FIREFOX_MULTILINE_VIEWPORT=1 plus existing INPUT/TEXT/MULTILINE flags, provider VIEWPORT/GEOMETRY capabilities and exact libxul build/instruction guards. Not an installed desktop default."
  },
